course: dictionary
lesson: 2357
title: Cubism: seeing from every side
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cubism is a style of painting and sculpture. You do not need to know it already: the sentence gives you clues. «Picasso was trained from a young child and could draw very realistically as a teenager; later he developed Cubism with Georges Braque, showing things from several sides at once.» Developed tells you Cubism was made by artists, and the last part tells you what makes it different: things are shown from several sides at once.
explain: Look for clue words. In Cubism, people and objects are shown as flat shapes, like cubes and angles. «Flat» and «shapes» tell you the picture is made of blocks, not soft curves. «Several sides at once» tells you the artist does not show just one view, as a camera would.
explain: Test your idea by swapping it into the sentence. Can you see the front, back and side of a cube at the same time? In Cubism, you can. A «Cubist» is an artist who works in this style.
fact: Cubism is a style of painting and sculpture.
fact: Cubism was begun around 1907–1908 by Pablo Picasso and Georges Braque.
fact: In Cubism, people and objects are shown as flat geometric shapes like cubes and angles.
fact: In Cubism, things are often seen from several sides at once.
fact: A «Cubist» is an artist who works in this style, and Cubism is linked to maths shapes.
exercise: «Later he developed Cubism with Georges Braque, showing things from several sides at once.» What does Cubism show? | Things in colour only | Things from one side only | *Things from several sides at once | Things that move
exercise: Who began Cubism with Pablo Picasso? | Leonardo da Vinci | *Georges Braque | Claude Monet
exercise: What is a Cubist? | A cook who makes cube-shaped cakes | *An artist who works in the Cubist style | A builder of square houses | A maths teacher who draws cubes
test: In Cubism, what shapes are people and objects made from? | Soft, round blobs | Long wavy lines | *Flat geometric shapes like cubes and angles | Tiny dots of light
test: Around which years was Cubism begun? | 1807–1808 | *1907–1908 | 1907–1970 | 1607–1608
exam: Which sentence best describes Cubism? | A kind of music played with blocks | *A style where things are shown as flat shapes, often from several sides at once | A style where artists only paint soft landscapes with one view | A type of photograph taken from far above
